{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAz9J7cMTHepwGUovQbi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The review-context area (ticket 11) is built, and every acceptance item has a real test that passes. Lint, typecheck and `npm run test:ts` (1051 assertions) pass, and so does the full `npm test`: every Go package plus the 22 launcher tests. All work is committed; only `.redeye/notes.md` is left out, as instructed.\n\nThe new code is in `src/context/`. It covers the reviewed tree and `pinIndexTree`, path confinement, blob reads from a pinned tree, `numberedSnippet` and `buildFileContext`, the whitespace normalizer, and the quote grounder. Tests are in `test/context/`.\n\nWhere I departed from the spec or had to interpret it:\n\n1. **Extra options argument.** Every function that runs git takes a trailing `{signal, env}` argument, so tests can pass an isolated repo environment and the CLI can pass its own. Ticket 10 did the same for `build`. The visible signature changes are `pinIndexTree(repo, signal, {env})`, which reads `GIT_INDEX_FILE` from that env, `resolveLive(repo, p, opts)` instead of taking a bare signal, and `newQuoteGrounder(..., opts)`, which takes its abort signal when it is created rather than on each call.\n2. **\"Injectable spawn\".** I used the method the repo already uses: a fake `git` placed first on the test env's `PATH` that records its process ID. The abort tests check that the call rejects with an `AbortError` and that the process is gone.\n3. **\"Live guard blocks exactly what pinning leaves out\".** This is compared over the test repo's file paths only. A symlink becomes an entry in a tree built with plain Git commands, so directories and symlinks are left out of the comparison. Whether snapshots keep symlinks is ticket 22's call.\n4. **File names with spaces don't ground against the diff.** Git adds a tab after a `---`/`+++` file name that contains a space, so the Go code files that diff section under `name<tab>` and quotes from it never match the real name. I kept this to match Go because it isn't one of the listed deliberate changes. It may be worth a follow-up.\n5. **Non-UTF-8 names in diff headers** are skipped rather than stored with replacement characters, so they fail closed.\n\nI also added a short section on the context area's conventions to `AGENTS.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":287,"cache_read_input_tokens":209785,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":287},"output_tokens":717,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2c0557b-d210-43b6-ab70-8720cf7cd94d","uuid":"3fd93f56-cea5-4645-b78e-aa1f969c62ca","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:59:11.046Z","request_id":"req_011ChAz9HpFP78ZUxFMQhbgz"}
